// PARAM: --analysis interval --context call-string --context-depth 2
// Adapted from Goblint tests/regression/32-widen-context/01-on.c
// (ana.context.widen enabled). f(x) recurses on x + 1 whenever x is
// nonzero, so f(1) never returns over VIMP's mathematical integers: the
// check after the call is dead and is suppressed (NOWARN). Goblint
// annotates the same check as proved because its C int wraps to 0 after
// overflow (or is widened to top, which its `!a` check tolerates); that is
// a semantic difference between C machine integers and VIMP's unbounded
// ints, not a precision difference. The bounded call string keeps the
// context space finite; under --context entry-state the same program
// creates a fresh context per x value and diverges, which
// 21-context-sensitivity/01-unbounded_context_chain_diverges.vimp pins
// through --timeout.
void f(x) {
  if (!(x == 0)) { r := f(x + 1); return r } else { return x }
}
void main() {
  a := f(1);
  __voblint_check(a == 0) // NOWARN
}
